 - [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and ASCII letter case before returning a matching record or NotFound.
 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
-- [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
-- [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or serial numbers that are equal after normalization, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records and its snapshot date together, without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL answer from the kiosk's local index file without network access.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL NOT match a record whose serial number differs from the query only in punctuation.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: If a snapshot import fails at any step, then the system SHALL delete the staging index file it created.
